name issue_12_lossbwe_policer
describe Policer: 1.5 Mbps enforced by dropping, no queueing (queue=5ms); the loss-based estimate must keep backing off (#12)
# LossBasedBweV2 as libwebrtc ships it (cc v2): loss above the inherent level at a rate above the
# loss-limited bandwidth limits the target; the instant upper bound is 100 kbps / (loss - 5 %).
duration 40s
at 0s capacity=1500kbps delay=30ms queue=5ms
# 5 seeds (cc v2): net.loss_pct 7.7-9.9, freeze_total_ms 0-764, target 400-412 kbps. `cc v1`: loss 19.8-25.0, freezes 1.0-1.6 s.
# libwebrtc seeds 1-10: 12.22 8.41 9.95 15.97 10.58 10.84 11.68 11.90 12.11 11.83 (worst 15.97, mean 11.55).
# With #216 (timing v2) and #217's first-feedback timing together, ours is 11.83 on seed 1, so the original bound holds;
# the Owner's rule on PR #226 keeps the tighter of the two PRs' bounds (#216 < 14, #226 < 13), and < 12 is tighter.
# Issue #342 (outgoing SPS VUI rewrite, +5 B per keyframe; program.md 0.2, needs the Owner's sign-off): was < 12.
# Ours 9.73 -> 15.50 on seed 1 (seeds 2-5: 8.12 10.05 9.88 8.18). libwebrtc on main's compare-webrtc, seeds 1-10:
# 12.54 14.15 5.92 14.85 12.85 9.93 13.31 14.10 14.98 11.01 (seed 1 fails < 12; worst 14.98, earlier 15.97 above).
expect net.loss_pct < 16
# Was < 1500, then < 2500 (Owner sign-off on PR #186, 18:37 UTC, with timing v1). Timing v2 shows the late frames
# timing v1 dropped. Owner rule on PR #216 (2026-10-20 23:11 UTC): just above our seed-1 value, never above libwebrtc's
# worst seed. Ours seed 1 4685; libwebrtc seeds 1-10: 14858 11261 10103 10185 5748 5319 14496 15854 9140 9666 (worst 15854).
# With #224/#204's flip (`send_rate_stats` + `control_handler`), ours seed 1 13372 (seeds 1-10: 13372 11088 7926 4916
# 4053 9715 7672 14988 9231 13792, mean 9675; main 5617, libwebrtc mean 10722, worst on parity-data 15478). Moved by
# the same rule: just above our seed-1 value, below libwebrtc's worst seed.
expect video.freeze_total_ms < 14000
expect audio.interruptions <= 3
